    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="1031" n="983" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v06p1/pg983"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, Eisenhower papers, Whitman
                    file</note>
                <head>No. 408<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum Prepared at the White
                        House</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d408-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-05-11">May 11, 1953</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Telephone calls—</p>
                <p>Beedle Smith called the President to report that just before leaving the country,
                    Mr. Dulles had received a cable from the Prime Minister saying that the P.M. was
                    going to report certain conversations that had been held between the two
                    countries in his speech before the House of Commons today.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d408-f2"/> Beedle Smith replied asking him not to do this.</p>
                <pb facs="1032" n="984" xml:id="pg984"/>
                <p>There was discussion of eventuality that the Pres. might have to tell the Prime
                    Minister that if discussions between the two countries were not held completely
                    confidential, they would have to cease.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d408-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d408-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably drafted by Ann Whitman, the President’s personal secretary.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d408-f2" n="2" xml:id="d408-f2-content">
                <p>Secretary Dulles left Washington for the Middle East at 7 p.m. on May 9; the
                    message from Churchill has not been further identified.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
